Example: `13-10-k3f7a2-2026`.

Rules:
1. Form: DD-MM-xxxxxx-YYYY
2. Day, month, year = date the entry is written
3. Six random lowercase letters and digits (mixed? "lowercase letters and digits" — alphabet [a-z0-9], exactly 6 chars)
4. Writers on different branches pick ids without coordination → never "next free number"
5. No two entries share an id
6. An id never changes → file keeps its name
7. Fails if: id not in W1.1 form; two entries share an id; git shows an entry file renamed to a different id.

